  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If electrolysis of aqueous CuSO $_{4}$ solution is carried out using Cu-electrodes, the reaction taking place at the anode is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zixgL",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{H}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LHlwS",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(\\mathrm{aq})+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{s})$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PeBc4",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}(\\mathrm{aq})-2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{SO}_{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eqcIr",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Cu}(\\mathrm{s})-2 e^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(\\mathrm{aq})$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Electrolysis of copper sulphate solution using Cu-electrodes, \r\nIons present : $\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}, \\mathrm{H}^{+}, \\mathrm{SO}_{4}^{2-}, \\mathrm{OH}^{-}$\r\nAt cathode $\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(a q)+2 e^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}(s)$\r\nAt anode $\\mathrm{Cu}(s)-2 e^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(a q)$\r\nSo, the option (d) is correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
